<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crete</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cretan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crete is the largest Greek island, in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>, home of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minoan-civilisation">Minoan civilisation</a>. Its ancient city-states were governed by magistrates called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosmoi">kosmoi</a>. Ancient writers, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristotle">Aristotle</a>, compared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>'s constitution with those of Crete and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, a comparison noted in the history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crete.jpg" alt="Crete" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ISS Expedition 28 crew · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Island_of_Crete,_Greece.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
